<article class="env-lemma" id="09EB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09EB">Lemma <span data-tag="09EB">15.114.2</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $K$. Let $L/K$ be a finite Galois extension. Then there are $e \geq 1$ and $f \geq 1$ such that $e_ i = e$ and $f_ i = f$ for all $i$ (notation as in Remark <a href="/tag/09E8" data-tag="09E8">15.113.6</a>). In particular $[L : K] = n e f$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Immediate consequence of Lemma <a href="/tag/09EA" data-tag="09EA">15.114.1</a> and the definitions. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>